
  riscvsim › demo 5 · Loops
  Add 1 to 10 and watch the counter count down.

   1  # Add 1 + 2 + ... + 10. x5 counts down from 10 and
   2  # x6 collects the sum; bne repeats until x5 is 0.
   3  addi x5, x0, 10    # counter
   4  addi x6, x0, 0     # sum
   5  loop:
   6  add  x6, x6, x5    # sum = sum + counter
   7  addi x5, x5, -1    # counter = counter - 1
   8  bne  x5, x0, loop  # again until the counter is 0

  cycle 1
    IF addi x5, x0, 10  ID ·  EX ·  MEM ·  WB ·
    counter x5 = 0 · sum x6 = 0
    › The first instruction, addi, is fetched from memory.

  cycle 2
    IF addi x6, x0, 0  ID addi x5, x0, 10  EX ·  MEM ·  WB ·
    counter x5 = 0 · sum x6 = 0
    › addi x5 is decoded and reads its source registers.

  cycle 3
    IF add x6, x6, x5  ID addi x6, x0, 0  EX addi x5, x0, 10  MEM ·  WB ·
    counter x5 = 0 · sum x6 = 0
    › addi x5 is computing in the ALU; everything else moves one stage on.

  cycle 4
    IF addi x5,x5,-1  ID add x6,x6,x5  EX addi x6,x0,0  MEM addi x5,x0…  WB ·
    counter x5 = 0 · sum x6 = 0
    › addi x6 is computing in the ALU; everything else moves one stage on.

  cycle 5
    IF bne x5,x0…  ID addi x5,x5…  EX add x6,x6…  MEM addi x6,x0…  WB addi x5…
    ✓ x5 = 10
    counter x5 = 10 · sum x6 = 0
    › add needs x6 from addi x6 and x5 from addi x5, so both are forwarded
      from pipeline registers and nobody waits.
      Forwarding: a result goes straight to the instruction that needs it,
      before it is written to its register.
      A pipeline register holds an instruction and its values between two
      stages.

  cycle 6
    IF ·  ID bne x5,x0…  EX addi x5,x5,-1  MEM add x6,x6,x5  WB addi x6,x0,0
    counter x5 = 10 · sum x6 = 0
    › addi finishes and writes x6 = 0.

  cycle 7
    IF ·  ID ·  EX bne x5, x0, loop  MEM addi x5, x5, -1  WB add x6, x6, x5
    ✓ x6 = 10
    counter x5 = 10 · sum x6 = 10
    › bne needs x5 from addi, so it is forwarded from the EX/MEM pipeline
      register and nobody waits.

  cycle 8
    IF add x6, x6, x5  ID flushed  EX ·  MEM bne x5,x0,loop  WB addi x5,x5,-1
    ✓ x5 = 9
    counter x5 = 9 · sum x6 = 10
    › addi finishes and writes x5 = 9.

  cycle 9
    IF addi x5,x5,-1  ID add x6, x6, x5  EX flushed  MEM ·  WB bne x5,x0,loop
    counter x5 = 9 · sum x6 = 10
    › add is decoded and reads its source registers.

  cycle 10
